      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OPS.SLK-C · Team Departure\n\nPOST `/webhook/team-departure` `{\"email\": \"...\"}` with header `x-departure-token: <SLACK_DEPARTURE_TOKEN>` → resolve the same channels B would have used → (live only) `conversations.kick` from each, `conversations.archive` the rep channel (never delete) → row `departed` → `#ops-alerts` with the manual-deactivation reminder.\n\n**Fail-closed auth.** The webhook is public, and kicking people is destructive, so it requires the token header. `SLACK_DEPARTURE_TOKEN` unset = every call gets 401. Set it before activating. (A Supabase DB webhook on status → departed can call this later.)\n\n**Slack cannot deactivate the account** on this plan (Enterprise-only API). Every summary ends with DEACTIVATE SLACK ACCOUNT MANUALLY — that is the human step.\n\n**No Slack id on the row** (never joined) → the row is still marked departed so a later stray join is refused by B, and #ops-alerts says nothing was removed.\n\n**Shadow mode** (`SLACK_ONBOARDING_MODE` ≠ live) evaluates everything and posts one `[SHADOW]` line; no kicks, no archive, no DB update.\n\n`Resolve Channels` embeds `scripts/lib/slack-onboarding-resolve.js` verbatim — the test suite checks it.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 820,
        "height": 500
      },
      "id": "df8fae50-6bb8-4ef2-acec-2bb6a280fbbd"
    },
